  "summary": "Install-time beacon exfiltrates host identifiers to hardcoded bare-IP endpoint",
  "details": "@ppa-web-components/ppa-hotel-collection@99.0.1 is a stub package whose main module exports a Proxy returning no-ops and whose declared postinstall script runs beacon.cjs. Both the postinstall and the main module's import-time code POST the installer's hostname, install path, current working directory, and node/npm version to a hardcoded plain-HTTP endpoint at http://185.158.107.175:8787/_ah/dc. The package advertises no functionality (description: \"Compatibility shim.\") and the implausibly high version (99.0.1) combined with the scoped stub shape is consistent with a dependency-confusion reconnaissance beacon targeting an internal package name.",
